        // Handle DeprecationWarning without suppressing it
        AppVersion appVersion2 = new AppVersion(1, 2, 3);
        appVersion2.printChangelist(); // This will throw a DeprecationWarning
    }
}
```

In this example, the `printChangelist()` method is marked as deprecated and throws a `DeprecationWarning` if called. The warning message is caught and printed to the console.

You can either suppress the warning using the `@SuppressWarnings("deprecation")` annotation or handle it without suppressing it by catching the `DeprecationWarning` exception.

Note that you can also use the `@Deprecated` annotation on classes or interfaces to mark them as deprecated, which means any subclass of those classes will automatically throw a `DeprecationWarning` when instantiated.
